file tools/crypto_monocypher_sha512_parity_witness.rish diffs the two byte-for-byte and anchors the two FIPS 180-4 known-answers — GREEN
file crypto/sha512.rye header note and GREEN selftest line moved Monocypher-source parity from held horizon to landed
file crypto/README.md the Monocypher-source parity list moved nine rungs → ten, naming standalone SHA-512
file docs/CRYPTO.md the parity paragraph moved nine rungs → ten, naming standalone SHA-512
recommend keep-going — an eleventh Monocypher one-shot (HMAC-SHA512 via crypto_sha512_hmac, or a crypto_verify16/32/64 constant-time-compare rung), or the docs-compression molt that feeds the seed; all gate-free and agent-doable.
